{"name":"Assault","hex":"#1c4374","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"assault","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A violent onset or attack with physical means, for example blows, weapons, etc.","A violent verbal attack, for example with insults, criticism, and the like"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To attack, physically or figuratively; to assail.","To threaten or harass. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/assault"}],"entries":[{"title":"Assault","blocks":[{"text":"In the terminology of law, an assault is the act of causing physical harm or unwanted physical contact to another person, or, in some legal definitions, the threat or attempt to do so. It is both a crime and a tort and, therefore, may result in criminal prosecution, civil liability, or both. Additionally, assault is a criminal act in which a person intentionally causes fear of physical harm or offensive contact to another person. Assault can be committed with or without a weapon and can range from physical violence to threats of violence. Assault is frequently referred to as an attempt to commit battery, which is the deliberate use of physical force against another person. The deliberate inflicting of fear, apprehension, or terror is another definition of assault that can be found in several legal systems. Depending on the severity of the offense, assault may result in a fine, imprisonment, or even death."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assault","wikidata":"Q365680"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Felony_Sentences_in_State_Courts.pdf/page1-500px-Felony_Sentences_in_State_Courts.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Felony_Sentences_in_State_Courts.pdf/page1-500px-Felony_Sentences_in_State_Courts.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Felony Sentences in State Courts, study by the United States Department of Justice","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFelony_Sentences_in_State_Courts.pdf"}],"sounds":{"assault":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c1/En-us-assault.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c1/En-us-assault.ogg/En-us-assault.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Hazy blue hour in Grand Canyon","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Hazy_blue_hour_in_Grand_Canyon.JPG/500px-Hazy_blue_hour_in_Grand_Canyon.JPG","ratio":1.4430577223088923,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hazy_blue_hour_in_Grand_Canyon.JPG","share":0.12},{"title":"20131003 Schoeningen Palaeon DSC08394 PtrQs","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/20131003_Schoeningen_Palaeon_DSC08394_PtrQs.jpg/500px-20131003_Schoeningen_Palaeon_DSC08394_PtrQs.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20131003_Schoeningen_Palaeon_DSC08394_PtrQs.jpg","share":0.11},{"title":"2018 01 (Blue) - Chaouen","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/2018_01_%28Blue%29_-_Chaouen.jpg/500px-2018_01_%28Blue%29_-_Chaouen.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2018_01_(Blue)_-_Chaouen.jpg","share":0.07},{"title":"Hinge on blue dumpster","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Hinge_on_blue_dumpster.jpg/500px-Hinge_on_blue_dumpster.jpg","ratio":1.3370226895406752,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hinge_on_blue_dumpster.jpg","share":0.06625},{"title":"WonderSwan-Color-Blue-Left","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/WonderSwan-Color-Blue-Left.jpg/500px-WonderSwan-Color-Blue-Left.jpg","ratio":1.4242424242424243,"link":"https://commons.wikimedi